Third-party notices
===================

NASA CEA thermochemistry tables
  propsim/core/thermo/data/cea_tables.npz contains combustion properties computed with
  NASA Chemical Equilibrium with Applications (CEA):
    S. Gordon and B. J. McBride, "Computer Program for Calculation of Complex Chemical
    Equilibrium Compositions and Applications", NASA Reference Publication 1311 (1994, 1996).
  The tables were generated by running CEA through RocketCEA (Applied Python, GPL-3.0).
  Neither CEA nor RocketCEA is distributed with PropSim; only the computed numbers are.

Component library (propsim/data/library)
  Machine-readable fluid, component, engine and cycle data, each value with its source, quality and location (see
  propsim/data/library/sources.csv and README.md). Sources and their terms:
    NASA SP-125, Huzel and Huang, "Design of Liquid Propellant Rocket Engines" - US Government work, public domain
    NASA SP-2009-4545, "Remembering the Giants: Apollo Rocket Propulsion Development" - US Government work, public domain
    NASA CEA thermodynamic database (Zehe, Gordon and McBride) - US Government work
    NIST Chemistry WebBook - NIST Standard Reference Data, each value citing its primary reference
    CoolProp 8.0.0 - MIT license; the property tables were regenerated with tools/build_fluid_tables.py
    L3Harris RL10 and RS-25 data sheets and web pages - single published numbers, cited with their location
  RocketProps (GPL-3.0) is an optional runtime backend only; none of its data is copied into the library.

